[AddtionalInformation]
; During various vehicle development runs, it is necessary to evaluate measurement data only at certain measuring points on the measurement track.
; For the above-mentioned purposes, 2D has developed the special CAL-Files 2D_GPSTracks, with which trigger positions are generated by the Latitude
; And Longitude channels during the analysis of the data, which can then be converted into various measurement tracks.
; The measuring points And tracks thus generated are thus much better suited in the Analyzer for linking to the actual vehicle measurement data
; And thus for further processing than the pure Latitude And Longitude values, since the measuring points And tracks are then available as individual channels.

; In this calculation file the trigger points, which were defined in a previous calculation file, are connected to measurement tracks.
; When executing this calculation file, channels (#GPSTrackNr, #GPSTrackNr_BIT, #GPSTrackNr_N) are created which are different parameters to describe the defined measurement tracks.

; For more detailed information about the functions of 2D_GPS_Pos_Office2D.CAL And 2D_GPS_Tracks_Office2D.CAL calculation files
; And how to use them, please see the detailed manual "2D_GPSTracks" at download area at our website https://2d-datarecording.com/en/downloads/manuals/

[Initializations]
GPSTrackNr          = Const(0,1000)                                             ; Initialize "GPSTrackNr"
GPSTrackNr_BIT      = Const(0,1000)                                             ; Initialize "GPSTrackNr_Bit"

[Call_function]

{$I <UserDataDir>\Calfiles\2DCalfiles\_2D_GPS_Track_InTrigger             , P(InKoordinate_1                                 , 1)}  ; GPSTrackNr_1 --> Point 1
{$I <UserDataDir>\Calfiles\2DCalfiles\_2D_GPS_Track_InTrigger_Course      , P(InKoordinate_2                      ,   88,  10, 2)}  ; GPSTrackNr_2 --> Point 2 with respect to Course
{$I <UserDataDir>\Calfiles\2DCalfiles\_2D_GPS_Track_BetweenTriggers       , P(AtKoordinate_4, AtKoordinate_3, 0, 0           , 3)}  ; GPSTrackNr_3 --> Point 3 to Point 4
{$I <UserDataDir>\Calfiles\2DCalfiles\_2D_GPS_Track_BetweenTriggers_Course, P(AtKoordinate_5, AtKoordinate_6, 0, 0,  165, 165, 4)}  ; GPSTrackNr_4 --> Point 5 to Point 6 with respect to Course


